title:    The denial this week rests on
subtitle: Attempted 2026-10-25 against the live organization. No key was created.
width:    1040
---
$ gcloud iam service-accounts keys create /tmp/should-not-exist.json \
    --iam-account=tf-plan@<SEED>.iam.gserviceaccount.com

ERROR: (gcloud.iam.service-accounts.keys.create) FAILED_PRECONDITION:
Operation denied by org policy on resource
'projects/-/serviceAccounts/<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ID>':
["constraints/iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation":
 "This constraint, when enforced, blocks service account key creation."]

- '@type': type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo
  domain: iam.googleapis.com
  metadata:
    customConstraints: constraints/iam.managed.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation
    resource: projects/-/serviceAccounts/<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ID>
  reason: CUSTOM_ORG_POLICY_VIOLATION

$ gcloud iam service-accounts keys list --managed-by=user \
    --iam-account=tf-plan@<SEED>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
(no rows)

# FAILED_PRECONDITION, not PERMISSION_DENIED - and that distinction is the
# whole point. An under-privileged attempt fails with a permission error that
# looks identical to the control working and proves nothing. This request
# passed the IAM check and was refused by the policy, which the error names.
